# Captain-triaged manifest for the --no-nix work-host path (see README.md).
# Install EXACTLY this, nothing more. Keep in sync with the "excluded by
# captain decision" list in README.md when either changes.
#
# Also the intent (not the manifest) for the codespace-work path: adding or
# removing a line here means work/codespace-bootstrap.sh needs the matching
# apt/npm/release-binary install too - see that file's header comment.
#
# Docker Desktop is deliberately absent and must stay absent: on the work
# Mac it is distributed through the company's Self-Service app, never
# Homebrew, so a `cask "docker-desktop"` line here would either fight the
# managed copy or install a second, unmanaged one. work/bootstrap.sh's
# check_docker instead looks for it at the end of a run and reports it as
# a pending item when it isn't there.

